# `*`, `/` and math functions of arrays are elementwise, so they fuse like
# `+` and `-`: `r` is one kernel of five operations (the `sqrt` included), and
# `q` of two. `s` is used twice and stays an array of its own.
x = [3 m, 6 m, 9 m]
y = [4 m, 8 m, 12 m]
k = 0.5
d = [1 m, 1 m, 1 m]
r = sqrt(x * x + y * y) * k + d
q = atan2(y, x) / [2, 2, 2]
s = hypot(x, y)
z = s * s / s + s
print(r, q, z)
